{% doc %}
  Emits <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow"> on OUT-OF-RANGE paginated
  URLs — /blogs/news?page=99, /collections/all?page=999, /search?q=x&page=50.

  Why: Shopify serves those with HTTP 200, a full layout, an empty result list and
  a self-referencing canonical. That is an unbounded set of thin, indexable URLs
  (anything can link ?page=<n> and Google will crawl and index it). Shopify gives
  the theme no way to return a real 404, so noindex is the available lever.

  This does NOT touch valid pages. Page 1 and every real paginated page stay fully
  indexable — including every page of the Journal and Brew Guides.

  Must render inside <head> — Google ignores a robots meta tag placed in <body>,
  which is why this cannot live in the paginated section itself where `paginate`
  is in scope. Since `paginate` is unreachable from the layout, the page count is
  recomputed here from the item total and the per-page size.

  The per-page size comes from snippets/paginate-page-size.liquid, which is the
  same snippet the paginated sections themselves read, so the two can never drift
  apart. Do not hardcode a page size here.

  SAFETY PROPERTY: the counts used here (blog.articles_count, collection.products_count,
  search.results_count) are always >= the number of items the section actually paginates
  — on a tag-filtered blog view, articles_count stays the blog total. So the computed
  page count can only ever be too HIGH, never too low. A wrong answer therefore means
  "failed to noindex a thin page" (harmless), never "noindexed a real page" (harmful).
  Preserve that direction if you change this.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign robots_total = nil

  case template.name
    when 'blog'
      assign robots_total = blog.articles_count
    when 'collection'
      assign robots_total = collection.products_count
    when 'search'
      assign robots_total = search.results_count
  endcase
-%}

{%- if robots_total != nil and current_page > 1 -%}
  {%- capture robots_per_page -%}{%- render 'paginate-page-size' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign robots_per_page = robots_per_page | strip | plus: 0
    comment
      A zero page size would make every page look out of range and noindex the whole
      template. Bail out rather than risk that.
    endcomment
    if robots_per_page > 0
      assign robots_max_page = robots_total | divided_by: robots_per_page
      assign robots_remainder = robots_total | modulo: robots_per_page
      if robots_remainder > 0
        assign robots_max_page = robots_max_page | plus: 1
      endif
      comment
        An empty blog/collection/search still has a legitimate page 1.
      endcomment
      if robots_max_page < 1
        assign robots_max_page = 1
      endif
      if current_page > robots_max_page
        echo '<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">'
      endif
    endif
  -%}
{%- endif -%}
